    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497-a2">

                <pb facs="0870" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg774"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Camp Grant</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 9,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To His Excellency Ignacio Pesquiera,
                        Governor of Sonora:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    after the 20th instant I will compel the Indians in the southern part of this
                    Territory, known as the tribe of Cochise, to <pb facs="0871" n="775"
                        xml:id="pg775"/> submit themselves to daily roll-call, and if they should
                    refuse I will commence hostilities against them without delay. Knowing that
                    these Indians have been a terrible scourge to your State, I take the liberty of
                    requesting you to place strong detachments near the line, to prevent them taking
                    refuge in Sonora if they escape the pursuit of our soldiers. Do me the favor to
                    keep this secret until the date mentioned above.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE CROOK,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brevet Brigadier-General,
                            United States Army.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
